Based on the stack trace and your reproduce case, what’s happening is that Cascader✱ (used by CascaderSelect) will, under the hood, write new properties (like its internal “pos”, “children” markers, etc.) directly onto each object in your `dataSource`.  In your example you are using Immer’s `produce` with `autoFreeze=true`, so every object in your state’s `data` array is frozen.  The moment Cascader tries to do something like

    item.pos = '0-1-2'

you get “Cannot add property … object is not extensible.”

The simplest way to work around this is to clone your entire `dataSource` right before handing it into Cascader, so that you’re mutating only the clone and not the frozen user data.  Here’s a *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch against **src/cascader-select/cascader-select.jsx** that

